### Kafka — topics and facts, via the Redpanda Console API
###
### The same data the Console UI shows at http://localhost:8080, but callable.
### This is where you SEE the domain facts the services publish: every saga
### step leaves one here.
###
### Requires: pnpm dc:up:infra

@console = http://localhost:8080

### All topics. Expect the six the kafka-init job derives from
### specs/shared/asyncapi.yaml — three fact topics and their .dlq companions:
###   otc.orders.facts.v1        otc.orders.facts.v1.dlq
###   otc.fulfillment.facts.v1   otc.fulfillment.facts.v1.dlq
###   otc.billing.facts.v1       otc.billing.facts.v1.dlq
GET {{console}}/api/topics

### One topic's configuration — partitions, replication, cleanup policy
GET {{console}}/api/topics/otc.orders.facts.v1

### THE FACTS THEMSELVES — the orders topic, newest first.
### Every message is an envelope: eventId, eventType, aggregateId,
### correlationId (the order id), causationId, occurredAt, payload.
GET {{console}}/api/topics/otc.orders.facts.v1/messages?pageSize=20

### Fulfillment's facts — stock.reserved.v1, stock.rejected.v1,
### stock.released.v1, order.despatched.v1
GET {{console}}/api/topics/otc.fulfillment.facts.v1/messages?pageSize=20

### Billing's facts — credit.approved.v1, credit.rejected.v1, credit.released.v1
### (and, from feature 21, invoice.issued.v1 / payment.received.v1)
GET {{console}}/api/topics/otc.billing.facts.v1/messages?pageSize=20

### The dead-letter topics. These should be EMPTY: nothing has been
### dead-lettered, and the retry/DLQ machinery itself lands in feature 27.
GET {{console}}/api/topics/otc.orders.facts.v1.dlq/messages?pageSize=10

### Consumer groups — the saga orchestrator's group appears here once
### apps/orders is running (Nest appends "-server" to the configured id).
GET {{console}}/api/consumer-groups
